  "id": "children-15-19",
  "stac_version": "1.1.0",
  "description": "Estimated number of children aged 15-19 per 100 m grid cell in Jamaica, 2020. Derived from the WorldPop Jamaica 100m Age structures in 2020 constrained dataset (id 50206) as m_15 + f_15 (WorldPop band 15 = ages 15-19, both sexes). National sum: 222,027 children (modelled). Modelled estimates, not a census count: WorldPop disaggregates census/projection totals to 100 m cells with a Random-Forest dasymetric model constrained to built settlements (Built-Settlement Growth Model). Values are fractional people per cell; NoData (-99999) marks cells mapped as unsettled. Native grid 3 arc-second (about 92 m north-south and 88 m east-west in Jamaica), EPSG:4326, 2880 x 1807 pixels, 106,310 settled pixels. WorldPop publishes five-year bands, so this raster includes 18- and 19-year-olds; an exact under-18 count cannot be derived from it.",
